10. GitHub

A new Git repository was created for Assignment 5 instead of continuing the Git history from the previous assignment.

The project was initialized, committed, connected to the new GitHub repository, and pushed to the main branch.

The main Git commands used were:

git init

git branch -M main

git add .

git commit -m "Complete Docker assignment"

git remote add origin <GitHub repository URL>

git push -u origin main

The complete project source code was uploaded to the new GitHub repository.

Screenshot: Insert a screenshot showing the Assignment 5 GitHub repository.

11. .gitignore

The .gitignore file is used to prevent unnecessary local files and sensitive configuration files from being uploaded to GitHub.

The following entries were used:

node_modules/
.env
venv/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

node_modules contains installed Node.js packages, while venv contains the local Python virtual environment.

The .env file is also ignored because it can contain sensitive information such as the MongoDB connection string.

The required project files such as the Dockerfiles, source code, docker-compose.yaml, package.json, package-lock.json, and requirements.txt are still included in the repository.

